traceability.evidence:
Key implementation and tests for docs/stories/002.0-DEV-ESLINT-CONFIG.story.md:

1) Flat ESLint v9 configuration linked to this story
- File: eslint.config.js
- Header:
  /**
   * ESLint flat config for Traceability Plugin
   * @story docs/stories/002.0-DEV-ESLINT-CONFIG.story.md
   * @req REQ-FLAT-CONFIG - Setup ESLint v9 flat config for plugin usage
   */
- Uses ESLint v9 flat config (array of config objects via module.exports = [ ... ])
- Integrates @eslint/js recommended base:
  const js = require("@eslint/js");
  module.exports = [
    js.configs.recommended,
    { files: ["*.config.js", ...], ... },
    { files: ["**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx"], languageOptions: { parser: typescriptParser, ... }, ... },
    { files: ["**/*.js", "**/*.jsx"], ... },
    { files: ["**/*.test.{js,ts,tsx}", ...], ... },
    { ignores: ["lib/**", "node_modules/**", "coverage/**", "docs/**", "*.md", ...] }
  ];
- Dynamically loads the plugin from ./src/index.js or ./lib/src/index.js with CI-aware error handling, so ESLint runs cleanly in dev and fails fast in CI when misconfigured.

2) Recommended and strict configuration presets (Core Functionality)
- File: src/index.ts
- Exports rule severities and config presets:
  const TRACEABILITY_RULE_SEVERITIES: Readonly<Record> = {
    "traceability/require-story-annotation": "error",
    "traceability/require-req-annotation": "error",
    "traceability/require-branch-annotation": "error",
    "traceability/valid-annotation-format": "warn",
    "traceability/valid-story-reference": "error",
    "traceability/valid-req-reference": "error",
  };

  function createTraceabilityFlatConfig() {
    return {
      plugins: { traceability: {} },
      rules: { ...TRACEABILITY_RULE_SEVERITIES },
    };
  }

  const configs = {
    recommended: [createTraceabilityFlatConfig()],
    strict: [createTraceabilityFlatConfig()],
  };

- Test: tests/plugin-default-export-and-configs.test.ts
  - Verifies default export contains rules and configs
  - Checks rule names list is correct
  - Asserts configs.recommended has:
    - traceability/require-story-annotation: "error"
    - traceability/require-req-annotation: "error"
    - traceability/require-branch-annotation: "error"
  - Asserts configs.strict contains same rules as recommended
  - Asserts valid-annotation-format is mapped to "warn" and others to "error"

3) Config validation and rule options for this story
- File: src/rules/valid-story-reference.ts
  - Defines configurable options and JSON-schema for the rule:
    meta: {
      schema: [
        {
          type: "object",
          properties: {
            storyDirectories: { type: "array", items: { type: "string" } },
            allowAbsolutePaths: { type: "boolean" },
            requireStoryExtension: { type: "boolean" },
          },
          additionalProperties: false,
        },
      ],
    }
  - Rule options read in create(context):
    const opts = context.options[0] as {
      storyDirectories?: string[];
      allowAbsolutePaths?: boolean;
      requireStoryExtension?: boolean;
    } | undefined;
    const storyDirs = opts?.storyDirectories || defaultStoryDirs;
    const allowAbsolute = opts?.allowAbsolutePaths || false;
    const requireExt = opts?.requireStoryExtension !== false;

- Direct tests tied to Story 002.0:
  File: tests/config/eslint-config-validation.test.ts
  /** @story docs/stories/002.0-DEV-ESLINT-CONFIG.story.md */
  describe("ESLint Configuration Setup (Story 002.0-DEV-ESLINT-CONFIG)", () => {
    it("[REQ-RULE-OPTIONS] rule meta.schema defines expected properties", () => {
      const schema = ((validStoryReference.meta as any).schema as any)[0];
      expect(schema.properties).toHaveProperty("storyDirectories");
      expect(schema.properties).toHaveProperty("allowAbsolutePaths");
      expect(schema.properties).toHaveProperty("requireStoryExtension");
    });

    it("[REQ-CONFIG-VALIDATION] schema disallows unknown options", () => {
      const schema = ((validStoryReference.meta as any).schema as any)[0];
      expect(schema.additionalProperties).toBe(false);
    });
  });

- Test execution:
  - Command run: npm test -- --runTestsByPath tests/config/eslint-config-validation.test.ts --verbose
  - Output:
    > eslint-plugin-traceability@1.0.5 test
    > jest --ci --bail --runTestsByPath tests/config/eslint-config-validation.test.ts --verbose
  - No error output or non-zero exit was reported by the runner tool, indicating the test completed successfully.

4) Customizable paths & rule options (REQ-CUSTOMIZABLE-PATHS, REQ-RULE-OPTIONS)
- Rule behaviour and options documented in:
