    - Describes storyDirectories, allowAbsolutePaths, requireStoryExtension and their semantics and defaults.
  - user-docs/api-reference.md under "traceability/valid-story-reference" and "traceability/valid-annotation-format" explicitly list per-rule configurable options and examples.

5) Project integration & flat-config best practices (REQ-FLAT-CONFIG, REQ-PROJECT-INTEGRATION)
- File: user-docs/eslint-9-setup-guide.md
  - Shows ESLint 9 flat config usage with js.configs.recommended and plugin integration:
    export default [
      js.configs.recommended,
      {
        files: ["**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx"],
        languageOptions: { parser: typescriptParser, parserOptions: { project: "./tsconfig.json", ... } },
        rules: { "@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars": "error" },
      },
      { files: ["**/*.js", "**/*.mjs"], ... },
      { files: ["**/*.test.{js,ts}", ...], globals: { describe, it, test, expect, ... } },
      { ignores: ["lib/**", "dist/**", "node_modules/**", "coverage/**"] },
    ];
  - Sections for:
    - JavaScript-only projects
    - TypeScript projects
    - Mixed JS/TS projects
    - Monorepos / workspaces
    - Test-files configuration
    - Troubleshooting ESLint Configuration (common issues & solutions)
  - Explicit integration snippet with this plugin:
    import js from "@eslint/js";
    import traceability from "eslint-plugin-traceability";
    export default [js.configs.recommended, traceability.configs.recommended];

- Files: README.md, user-docs/examples.md, docs/config-presets.md, user-docs/api-reference.md
  - README: Quick Start and example eslint.config.js using traceability.configs.recommended.
  - docs/config-presets.md: documents recommended & strict presets and how to combine with @eslint/js.
  - examples.md: runnable examples for recommended and strict presets with flat config.
  - api-reference.md: dedicated "Configuration Presets" section mirroring the code-level presets.

- ESLint CLI integration test:
  File: tests/integration/cli-integration.test.ts
  - Uses ESLint CLI with the project eslint.config.js to run plugin rules via --config configPath.
  - Confirms plugin works end-to-end with ESLint CLI and flat config, validating plugin registration and behavior under a realistic configuration.

6) Error handling for configuration (REQ-CONFIG-VALIDATION, Error Handling acceptance criterion)
- Rule-level configuration validation:
  - As shown above, valid-story-reference provides a strict JSON schema with additionalProperties: false; the tests assert this behavior.
  - This causes ESLint to emit clear configuration errors for unknown or mis-typed options.

- Plugin loading error handling in eslint.config.js:
  - Tries ./src/index.js, then ./lib/src/index.js.
  - In CI: throws a clear error if the plugin cannot be found, failing fast.
  - In local dev: logs a warning and falls back to an empty plugin object so ESLint can still run without traceability rules.

7) Documentation and troubleshooting (User Experience & Documentation acceptance criteria)
- user-docs/eslint-9-setup-guide.md contains:
  - "Common Configuration Patterns" (JS-only, TS, mixed, monorepo, tests)
  - "Common Issues and Solutions" and "Troubleshooting ESLint Configuration" explicitly covering typical misconfigurations and fixes.
- README.md and user-docs/examples.md provide clear step-by-step setup, usage, and configuration snippets for flat config and presets.
- docs/config-presets.md clearly describes recommended vs strict presets, their rule severities, and usage examples.

